<title>RUSSIA: Rouble edges down on T-bill profit-taking,reserves.</title>
<headline>Rouble edges down on T-bill profit-taking,reserves.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rouble edged down on Wednesday on the continuing impact of the May 1 reduction in rouble reserve requirements, and demand for dollars on profit-taking in government securities.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	May 14 midday  May 14 early   May 13 close</p>
<p> today settlement    5,757-59	 5,757-59	 5,755-57</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement 5,757-59	 5,757-59	 5,754-55</p>
<p> overnight credit (%)    5-15	     5-15	     5-10</p>
<p>			   May 14				May 13</p>
<p> central bank	  5,750/92			    5,750/92</p>
<p> MICEX		   5,756				 5,751</p>
<p>&quot;The dollar edged up as there are more roubles on the market (after the cut in requirements),&quot; a Mezhkombank dealer said.</p>
<p>Inkombank dealer Vladislav Savelyev said higher dollar demand could be due to profit-taking of investing in Treasury bills and OFZ bonds.</p>
<p>--Anna Smirnova, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
</text>
